I don't think so.

It used to be that unicorns dropped a horn every time you killed one,
but the code was changed so that the chances are much less for revived
critters (something like 1/20).  If you google for "unicorn horn
farming" or similar, there was a short thread a year or two ago that
dicsussed this.  I believe the code was also changed to make it more
unlikely to get dragon scales by killing/reviving.

So, you can still kill for horns, it just takes a lot longer.  My
primary goal in the last few sessions has been trying to boost my
Power points, so that I can go longer between "recharges" (confused
scrolls of charging).  I've now just about got it to the "break even"
point, whereby on average I produce enough magic markers to write the
scrolls of charging :) (otherwise, I just sit around for 2000 turns,
but then that uses up your spell time, and spell books, etc.)

Of course, a couple of versions earlier (when I had the time to do
most of my ascensions to date), you could get magic markers from
polypiling any ol' tools, and this collection of unicorn horns wasn't
necessary.  I always enjoyed, in the games I found Ludios, dragging
all the tools to that level, and polypiling them along with all the
untrapped land mines :)

